# core.autocrlf is true on the development machine and this repo had no
# attributes file, so git would rewrite the beads export to CRLF on the next
# checkout while `bd export` keeps emitting LF. The Stop hook in
# .claude/hooks/check-beads.sh compares the two byte for byte to decide whether
# the tracked export has drifted, so that mismatch would make it rewrite the
# file and warn on EVERY turn -- a hook that always fires is a hook that gets
# switched off. It is generated data; nothing wants it line-ending-normalised.
.beads/issues.jsonl -text
